Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation ... # TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\n\nBack ArXiv cs.CV TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\n\nArXiv cs.CV\n\n# TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\n\nBohao Tang, Fei Zhang, Frost Xu, Hang Li, Pengfei Liu, Semih Gunel, Sen He, Soubhik Sanyal +4 more\n\n2603.17944 Published Mar 18, 2026\n\nChat with paper Cite 中文 View PDF Share\n\n### Publication\n\nPublished: Mar 18, 2026\n\nCategories: cs.CV\n\n### Metrics\n\nSource: ArXiv\n\n### Paper Preview\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe introduce the first method, to the best of our knowledge, for adapting image-to-video models to layer-aware text (glyph) animation, a capability critical for practical dynamic visual design. Existing approaches predominantly handle the transparency-encoding (alpha channel) as an extra latent dimension appended to the RGB space, necessitating the reconstruction of the underlying RGB-centric variational autoencoder (VAE). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVisual frame-wise results of our image-to-video (I2V) RGBA glyph... | Download Scientific Diagram (https://www.researchgate.net/figure/sual-frame-wise-results-of-our-image-to-video-I2V-RGBA-glyph-animation-model-TransText_fig1_402739516)\nciteturn40479search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\n\nFigure 1 - available via license: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International\n\nContent may be subject to copyright.\n\nDownload\n\nView publication\n\nImage: Visual frame-wise results of our image-to-video (I2V) RGBA glyph animation model. TransText generates diverse and complex glyph animations with accurate, clean transparency while strictly preserving the style of the reference image. See the Supplementary Materials for additional video results.\n\n# Visual frame-wise results of our image-to-video (I2V) RGBA glyph animation model. TransText generates diverse and complex glyph animations with accurate, clean transparency while strictly preserving the style of the reference image. See the Supplementary Materials for additional video results.\n\nSource publication\n\nTransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\n\nPreprint\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Mar 2026\n\n  * Fei Zhang\n  * Zijian Zhou\n  * Bohao Tang\n  * [...]\n  * Semih Gunel\n\nWe introduce the first method, to the best of our knowledge, for adapting image-to-video models to layer-aware text (glyph) animation, a capability critical for practical dynamic visual design. Existing approaches predominantly handle the transparency-encoding (alpha channel) as an extra latent dimension appended to the RGB space, necessitating the...\n\nCite\n\nDownload full-text\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDaily arXiv Papers - 2026-03-19 (https://blog.yueqianlin.com/daily-publication/260319/)\nciteturn40479search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; ## [253] TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\nExperimental results on C-TRAIL and MM-AU show that our method outperforms general and legal LLMs, as well as existing agent-based approaches, while providing a transparent and interpretable legal reasoning process.\n\n## [253] TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\n\nFei Zhang, Zijian Zhou, Bohao Tang, Sen He, Hang Li, Zhe Wang, Soubhik Sanyal, Pengfei Liu, Viktar Atliha, Tao Xiang, Frost Xu, Semih Gunel\n\nMain category: cs.CV\n\nTL;DR: TransText: A framework for adapting image-to-video models to layer-aware text animation using Alpha-as-RGB paradigm without modifying pre-trained generative models.\n\nDetailsMotivation: Existing methods for transparent glyph animation require reconstructing RGB-centric VAEs, which is computationally expensive and risks losing semantic priors from RGB data. There's a need for efficient adaptation of image-to-video models to handle transparency without compromising existing capabilities.\n\nMethod: Proposes TransText with Alpha-as-RGB paradigm that embeds alpha channel as RGB-compatible visual signal through latent spatial concatenation. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n#acmmm2026 #meta #metaresearch #videogeneration #generativeai #computervision #typography #transtext | Fei Zhang (https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ferenas97_acmmm2026-meta-metaresearch-activity-7481391968951021572-_Fx-)\nciteturn40479search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; I’m incredibly excited to share that our paper, \"TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\", has just been accepted to ACM Multimedia (ACM MM) 2026!\n\nFei Zhang\n\n1w Edited\n\nI’m incredibly excited to share that our paper, \"TransText: Transparency Aware Image-to-Video Typography Animation\", has just been accepted to ACM Multimedia (ACM MM) 2026! 🎉 This research was conducted during my 1st internship at Meta, and it marks a deeply special milestone for me as my very first work in the video generation field! 🎬 A huge shoutout and heartfelt thanks to my amazing colleagues (Semih Günel, Mengmeng Xu, Zijian Zhou, Zhe Wang, Sen He, Viktar Atliha, Soubhik S., Hang Li, Tao Xiang) at Meta. Thank you for your invaluable guidance, insightful discussions, and for providing such a fantastic environment for cutting-edge research. This milestone wouldn't have been possible without your continuous support and belief in me! --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · MoonshotAI/Kimi-K2.5 · GitHub (https://github.com/MoonshotAI/Kimi-K2.5/releases)\nciteturn40479view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/MoonshotAI/Kimi-K2.5/releases\